' The project's startup object, and nothing else.
'
' Every project gets its Sub Main from here. A sample may declare its own Main
' as well -- two Public Sub Mains in different modules compile -- so a page's
' `Module Startup` sample compiles as written, and nothing renames or refuses it.
'
' Compiling is all check_examples asks. A BUILD is different: binding the startup
' object fails with "'Main' is ambiguous", so tbrun never runs the probe. A tree
' for tbrun whose own module declares Sub Main leaves this file out. Measured on
' BETA 983, when two of round 10's executed cases failed that way.
'
' It is deliberately empty. The HelloWorld template's Main is a MsgBox, and a
' MsgBox hangs a run-mode probe invisibly -- the IDE waits on a modal nobody can
' see, on a desktop nobody can reach.

Module tbxMain

    Public Sub Main()
    End Sub

End Module
